# Resource template

Part of the [[README]]. Skeleton for a new Resource in `Resources/`. Rules: [[organization]], [[schema]], [[body-sections]].

**Using it:** [[= owner =]] creates a new file in `Resources/`, and Templater fills it. Agents copy it by hand and save it as `Resources/<slug>.md`. Both, in detail: [[template-task]]. Then:

- Set `type` ([[schema]] defines each).
- Optional fields: [[schema]].
- Add `people:` only for someone other than [[= owner =]].
- Link it from the task that needs it, in the same change ([[linking]]).
- Replace the Summary heading with sections the material needs.

<%*
tR = "";
let title = tp.file.title;
if (title.startsWith("Untitled")) title = await tp.system.prompt("Resource title (sentence case)");
const slug = title.normalize("NFKD").replace(/[^\x00-\x7F]/g, "").toLowerCase().replace(/'/g, "").replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, "-").replace(/^-+|-+$/g, "");
await tp.file.move("Resources/" + slug);
-%>
